# Service identity declaration: slurm:153. New Saphira allocation in
# the 0..199 package range for the Slurm daemons (SlurmUser=slurm):
# first free ID above the highest claimed identity (152 udpdist),
# clear of systemd's reserved block (127-131, 144, 145), and proven
# against the full union (base-seed accounts.tsv plus every recipe
# fragment) after 111 collided with base-seed chrony at the sign gate.
# The name is plain `slurm` (no underscore prefix) to match SlurmUser
# and the compiled-in defaults; renaming would force SlurmUser
# overrides everywhere for no gain.
# Single owner: the slurm package; slurm-accounting depends on slurm
# so the identity exists before slurmdbd is installed.
user slurm 153 slurm /var/lib/slurm /sbin/nologin
group slurm 153
dir /var/spool/slurmctld 0755 slurm slurm
dir /var/spool/slurmd 0755 root root
dir /var/log/slurm 0755 slurm slurm
